Cell["SpectralElement`", "ContextNameCell"],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{{Cell["SpectralNDSolve", "ObjectName"]}}]], "ObjectNameGrid",
  CellID->200000044],
Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{{"", Cell[TextData[{
  Cell[BoxData["SpectralNDSolve[eq, u, {x, y} ∈ Ω, n, opts]"], "InlineFormula"],
  " \[LineSeparator]",
  "SpectralNDSolve[eq, u, {x, y} ∈ Ω, n, opts] solves a partial differential equation for u on the domain Ω using the multi-domain spectral-element method with degree n per patch, and returns the result in the same {{u -> ...}} form as NDSolve, wrapped in a single pair of braces.  Ω is a CoonsPatch list, a SpectralDiscretization, or a region shorthand (Rectangle or Annulus).  eq may contain DirichletCondition terms; if none is given, homogeneous Dirichlet data is imposed on the whole boundary.  Linear problems are solved directly; nonlinear ones by Newton's method (Method -> \"Newton\", the default when the equations are nonlinear).  Returns {{u -> Function[...]{...}}}."
}]]}}]], "Usage", CellID->982511436]
}, Open]],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["Details and Options"], "NotesSection",
  WholeCellGroupOpener->True, CellGroupingRules->{"SectionGrouping", 50},
  CellID->200000045],
Cell[BoxData["SpectralNDSolve returns the solution in the same shape as NDSolve: a list
          containing a single list of rules, {{u -> Function[...]}}. Use
          SpectralNDSolveValue for the function itself."], "Notes", CellID->200000046],
Cell[BoxData["Ω may be a list of CoonsPatch objects, an already-built
          SpectralDiscretization -- which is consumed as-is and never rebuilt, which
          is the reason the discretization layer is public -- or a region shorthand.
          n is the polynomial degree of every patch, an integer >= 2."], "Notes", CellID->200000047],
Cell[BoxData["The Laplacian term is recognized in either sign, because the kernel
          rewrites Laplacian[u[x, y], {x, y}] into pure-derivative terms and the
          parser matches on those. DirichletCondition terms in the same list are
          honoured, each contributing one boundary predicate plus a value."], "Notes", CellID->200000048],
Cell[BoxData["With no DirichletCondition in the equation list, homogeneous Dirichlet
          data u == 0 is imposed on the whole exterior boundary. That path is exact:
          u is 0 at the boundary, not merely small."], "Notes", CellID->200000049],
Cell[BoxData["Options"], "NotesHead", CellID->200000050],
Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{{"{\"Method\", \"Automatic\"} (default)",
   "dispatches on the equation: LinearSolve when nothing is nonlinear in u, Newton's method otherwise. \"Linear\" and \"Newton\" force one. Any other value is refused with SpectralNDSolve::method"},
{"{\"MaxIterations\", 30} (default)",
   "the Newton iteration cap. It is honoured: MaxIterations -> 1 cannot converge the nonlinear problem and the call returns $Failed with SpectralNDSolve::nlnum rather than a wrong answer"},
{"{\"Tolerance\", \"AccuracyGoal\", \"PrecisionGoal\"}",
   "resolved in that order, then the solver's own 1*^-13. Newton stops when the step norm or the residual norm drops below it"},
{"{\"DomainOptions\", {}} (default)",
   "handed straight to SpectralDomain when the solver builds the discretization itself. Not consulted when Ω is already a SpectralDiscretization"}}]], "Notes", CellID->200000051],
Cell[BoxData["The assembled operator is +Laplacian, so a PDE written −Laplacian[u] + u^3
          == f assembles with OpCoefficient = −1 and the sign is applied in exactly
          one place in the code."], "Notes", CellID->200000052],
Cell[BoxData["The returned interpolant takes scalars. Function[{qx, qy}, ...] returns
          Indeterminate for anything non-numeric, which means a bare expr /@ points
          silently asks for f[point1, point2, ...] and gets nothing back. Write
          Function[...] & /@ points, or Apply[f, pts, {1}]."], "Notes", CellID->200000053],
Cell[BoxData["Messages"], "NotesHead", CellID->200000054],
Cell[BoxData["SpectralNDSolve::nlnum -- Newton did not converge; the message carries the
          iteration count, the last step norm, the tolerance, the last residual norm
          and the tolerance again. SpectralNDSolve::method -- an unknown Method
          value. SpectralNDSolve::nlift -- a DirichletCondition value did not
          evaluate to numbers, naming the number of offending boundary nodes. That
          is a refusal by contract, not a limitation to work around: silently
          zeroing the boundary is how a PDE solver produces a confidently wrong
          answer."], "Notes", CellID->200000055]
}, Open]],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData[{"Examples", "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]", Cell["(1)", "ExampleCount"]}],
  "PrimaryExamplesSection", CellTags->"PrimaryExamplesSection",
  CellID->200000056],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["Basic Examples"], "ExampleSection", "ExampleSection",
  WholeCellGroupOpener->True, CellID->200000057],
Cell["Load the package.", "ExampleText", CellID->200000058],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["Needs[\"SpectralElement`\"];
None"], "Input", CellLabel->"In[1]:=", CellID->200000059]
}, Open]],
Cell["A manufactured solution and its boundary data. uexz is an exact solution
      of −Laplacian[u] == fLin, so the difference between the returned
      interpolant and uexz is a genuine numerical error and nothing else. bd
      must name every side of the boundary: a side that is missed falls back
      to u == 0, which uexz does not satisfy, and the error is O(1) and does
      not shrink with the degree.", "ExampleText", CellID->200000060],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["uexz[x_, y_] := Sin[2 x + 1] Cos[3 y - 1] + x y/5;
fLin = -Laplacian[uexz[x, y], {x, y}];
bd = Abs[x + 1.5] < 1.*^-8 || Abs[x - 1.8] < 1.*^-8 ||
     Abs[y + 1.2] < 1.*^-8 || Abs[y - 1.3] < 1.*^-8;
None"], "Input", CellLabel->"In[2]:=", CellID->200000061]
}, Open]],
Cell["Solve a linear Poisson problem on a rectangle at degree 16. The answer
      has the NDSolve shape: one rule, u mapped to a function.", "ExampleText", CellID->200000062],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["sol = SpectralNDSolve[{-Laplacian[u[x, y], {x, y}] == fLin,
       DirichletCondition[u[x, y] == uexz[x, y], bd]}, u,
     {x, y} ∈ Rectangle[{-1.5, -1.2}, {1.8, 1.3}], 16];
MatchQ[sol, {{u -> _Function}}]"], "Input", CellLabel->"In[3]:=", CellID->200000063],
Cell[BoxData["\"True\""], "Output", CellLabel->"Out[4]=", CellID->200000064]
}, Open]],
Cell["And the solved-for symbol is the u that went in.", "ExampleText", CellID->200000065],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["sol[[1, 1, 1]]"], "Input", CellLabel->"In[5]:=", CellID->200000066],
Cell[BoxData["\"u\""], "Output", CellLabel->"Out[6]=", CellID->200000067]
}, Open]],
Cell["Evaluate the interpolant. The exact value is −0.03; the residual
      difference is the truncation error at degree 16.", "ExampleText", CellID->200000068],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["{sol[[1, 1, 2]][-0.5, 0.3], N[uexz[-0.5, 0.3]]}"], "Input", CellLabel->"In[7]:=", CellID->200000069],
Cell[BoxData["RowBox[{\"{\", RowBox[{RowBox[{\"-\", \"0.02999999999604433`\"}], \",\", RowBox[{\"-\", \"0.03`\"}]}], \"}\"}]"], "Output", CellLabel->"Out[8]=", CellID->200000070]
}, Open]],
Cell["The largest error over five interior points.", "ExampleText", CellID->200000071],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["uf = sol[[1, 1, 2]];
Max[Abs[uf @@ # - uexz @@ #] & /@ {{-0.5, 0.3}, {0.1, 0.2},
     {-0.4, 0.6}, {0.9, -0.7}, {0.6, 0.8}}]"], "Input", CellLabel->"In[9]:=", CellID->200000072],
Cell[BoxData["\"2.7444280181754266`*^-10\""], "Output", CellLabel->"Out[10]=", CellID->200000073]
}, Open]],
Cell["Adding u^3 to the left-hand side forces the Newton path. The answer has
      the same shape.", "ExampleText", CellID->200000074],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["fNl = fLin + uexz[x, y]^3;
solNl = SpectralNDSolve[{-Laplacian[u[x, y], {x, y}] + u[x, y]^3 == fNl,
        DirichletCondition[u[x, y] == uexz[x, y], bd]}, u,
      {x, y} ∈ Rectangle[{-1.5, -1.2}, {1.8, 1.3}], 16];
MatchQ[solNl, {{u -> _Function}}]"], "Input", CellLabel->"In[11]:=", CellID->200000075],
Cell[BoxData["\"True\""], "Output", CellLabel->"Out[12]=", CellID->200000076]
}, Open]],
Cell["MaxIterations is honoured, and the test for that is sharp: one iteration
      cannot converge this problem, so the call returns $Failed with the
      iteration count, the last step norm and the last residual norm in the
      message. A dropped option would return a solution instead.", "ExampleText", CellID->200000077],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["SpectralNDSolve[{-Laplacian[u[x, y], {x, y}] + u[x, y]^3 == fNl,
        DirichletCondition[u[x, y] == uexz[x, y], bd]}, u,
      {x, y} ∈ Rectangle[{-1.5, -1.2}, {1.8, 1.3}], 16,
      MaxIterations -> 1]"], "Input", CellLabel->"In[13]:=", CellID->200000078],
Cell[BoxData["\"$Failed\""], "Output", CellLabel->"Out[14]=", CellID->200000079]
}, Open]],
Cell["Method -> \"Newton\" reproduces the automatic dispatch bit for bit: the
      two interpolants agree at every sampled point, to 0. exactly.", "ExampleText", CellID->200000080],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["ufNl = solNl[[1, 1, 2]];
solNewton = SpectralNDSolve[{-Laplacian[u[x, y], {x, y}] + u[x, y]^3 == fNl,
        DirichletCondition[u[x, y] == uexz[x, y], bd]}, u,
      {x, y} ∈ Rectangle[{-1.5, -1.2}, {1.8, 1.3}], 16,
      Method -> \"Newton\"];
ufNew = solNewton[[1, 1, 2]];
Max[Abs[ufNew @@ # - ufNl @@ #] & /@ {{-0.5, 0.3}, {0.1, 0.2},
     {-0.4, 0.6}, {0.9, -0.7}, {0.6, 0.8}}]"], "Input", CellLabel->"In[15]:=", CellID->200000081],
Cell[BoxData["\"0.`\""], "Output", CellLabel->"Out[16]=", CellID->200000082]
}, Open]],
Cell["A SpectralDiscretization may be handed in instead of a region, and is
      consumed as-is -- which is what makes the discretization layer public.", "ExampleText", CellID->200000083],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["disc12 = SpectralDomain[Rectangle[{-1.5, -1.2}, {1.8, 1.3}], 12];
solD = SpectralNDSolve[{-Laplacian[u[x, y], {x, y}] == fLin,
       DirichletCondition[u[x, y] == uexz[x, y], bd]}, u, {x, y} ∈ disc12, 12];
Abs[solD[[1, 1, 2]][0.1, 0.2] - uexz[0.1, 0.2]]"], "Input", CellLabel->"In[17]:=", CellID->200000084],
Cell[BoxData["\"1.2541848011249357`*^-6\""], "Output", CellLabel->"Out[18]=", CellID->200000085]
}, Open]],
Cell["An unknown method name is refused, never downgraded.", "ExampleText", CellID->200000086],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["SpectralNDSolve[{-Laplacian[u[x, y], {x, y}] == fLin,
       DirichletCondition[u[x, y] == uexz[x, y], bd]}, u,
     {x, y} ∈ Rectangle[{-1.5, -1.2}, {1.8, 1.3}], 12,
     Method -> \"NoSuchMethod\"]"], "Input", CellLabel->"In[19]:=", CellID->200000087],
Cell[BoxData["\"$Failed\""], "Output", CellLabel->"Out[20]=", CellID->200000088]
}, Open]],
Cell["A curved domain, built from the region shorthand Annulus[{1, 2}, {0,
      Pi}]. bdAnn names the two circular arcs and the straight edge on y = 0;
      a manufactured solution that omits the straight edge measures an error
      of exactly Cos[1] = 0.54, which is a good way to see why the predicate
      has to be complete.", "ExampleText", CellID->200000089],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["bdAnn = Abs[Sqrt[x^2 + y^2] - 1] < 1.*^-8 || Abs[Sqrt[x^2 + y^2] - 2] < 1.*^-8 ||
        Abs[y] < 1.*^-8;
solA = SpectralNDSolve[{-Laplacian[u[x, y], {x, y}] == fLin,
       DirichletCondition[u[x, y] == uexz[x, y], bdAnn]}, u,
     {x, y} ∈ Annulus[{1, 2}, {0, Pi}], 16];
MatchQ[solA, {{u -> _Function}}]"], "Input", CellLabel->"In[21]:=", CellID->200000090],
Cell[BoxData["\"True\""], "Output", CellLabel->"Out[22]=", CellID->200000091]
}, Open]],
Cell["Evaluating on the annular sector. The error is set by the geometry -- an
      annular sector is not a polynomial image of a square -- not by the
      solver, and it converges with degree.", "ExampleText", CellID->200000092],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["solA[[1, 1, 2]][1.5, 0]"], "Input", CellLabel->"In[23]:=", CellID->200000093],
Cell[BoxData["RowBox[{\"-\", \"0.4089021333016357`\"}]"], "Output", CellLabel->"Out[24]=", CellID->200000094]
}, Open]],
Cell["With no DirichletCondition at all, u == 0 is imposed on the whole
      exterior boundary. poly vanishes on all four edges of the square, so the
      closed form is consistent with the default data and the boundary values
      come back exactly 0., not merely small.", "ExampleText", CellID->200000095],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["poly[a_, b_] := (1 - a^2) (1 - b^2);
noDc = SpectralNDSolve[{-Laplacian[u[x, y], {x, y}] == -Laplacian[poly[x, y], {x, y}]}, u,
    {x, y} ∈ Rectangle[{-1, -1}, {1, 1}], 12];
Apply[noDc[[1, 1, 2]], {{1., 0.}, {-1., 0.}, {0., 1.}, {0., -1.}}, {1}]"], "Input", CellLabel->"In[25]:=", CellID->200000096],
Cell[BoxData["RowBox[{\"{\", RowBox[{\"0.`\", \",\", \"0.`\", \",\", \"0.`\", \",\", \"0.`\"}], \"}\"}]"], "Output", CellLabel->"Out[26]=", CellID->200000097]
}, Open]],
Cell["The interior still reproduces poly, to round-off: poly is degree 2 per
      variable, well inside the degree-12 discrete space, so this is the floor
      rather than a truncation error.", "ExampleText", CellID->200000098],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["uf0 = noDc[[1, 1, 2]];
Max[Abs[uf0 @@ # - poly @@ #] & /@ {{0.25, 0.5}, {-0.5, -0.25},
     {0.6, -0.7}, {0., 0.}}]"], "Input", CellLabel->"In[27]:=", CellID->200000099],
Cell[BoxData["\"2.886579864025407`*^-15\""], "Output", CellLabel->"Out[28]=", CellID->200000100]
}, Open]],
Cell["Dirichlet data that is not a number is refused by name rather than
      guessed at: SpectralNDSolve::nlift counts the offending boundary nodes
      and the call returns $Failed.", "ExampleText", CellID->200000101],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["gd[a_, b_] := gUndefined[a, b];
SpectralNDSolve[{-Laplacian[u[x, y], {x, y}] == 1,
    DirichletCondition[u[x, y] == gd[x, y],
      Abs[x] < 1.*^-8 || Abs[x - 1.] < 1.*^-8 || Abs[y] < 1.*^-8 || Abs[y - 1.] < 1.*^-8]},
  u, {x, y} ∈ Rectangle[{-1, -1}, {1, 1}], 12]"], "Input", CellLabel->"In[29]:=", CellID->200000102],
Cell[BoxData["\"$Failed\""], "Output", CellLabel->"Out[30]=", CellID->200000103]
}, Open]],
Cell["Finally the curved patch from the README quickstart: four concave
      quadratic arcs, each side pushed inward by 0.4 at its midpoint.", "ExampleText", CellID->200000104],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["gamma = 0.4;
bot = Function[t, {t, -1 + gamma (1 - t^2)}];
top = Function[t, {t,  1 - gamma (1 - t^2)}];
lef = Function[t, {-1 + gamma (1 - t^2), t}];
rig = Function[t, { 1 - gamma (1 - t^2), t}];
cpatch = CoonsPatch[{bot, top, lef, rig}];
uex2[x_, y_] := Sin[2 x + 1] Cos[3 y - 1] + x y/5;
fL2 = -Laplacian[uex2[x, y], {x, y}];
onPatch = Abs[y + 1 - gamma (1 - x^2)] < 1.*^-8 || Abs[y - 1 + gamma (1 - x^2)] < 1.*^-8 ||
         Abs[x + 1 - gamma (1 - y^2)] < 1.*^-8 || Abs[x - 1 + gamma (1 - y^2)] < 1.*^-8;
None"], "Input", CellLabel->"In[31]:=", CellID->200000105]
}, Open]],
Cell["Solve on it, and evaluate at the centre.", "ExampleText", CellID->200000106],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["solC = SpectralNDSolve[{-Laplacian[u[x, y], {x, y}] == fL2,
      DirichletCondition[u[x, y] == uex2[x, y], onPatch]}, u, {x, y} ∈ {cpatch}, 14];
solC[[1, 1, 2]][0, 0]"], "Input", CellLabel->"In[32]:=", CellID->200000107],
Cell[BoxData["\"0.4546487121705494`\""], "Output", CellLabel->"Out[33]=", CellID->200000108]
}, Open]],
Cell["The exact value there is 0.4546487134128409, so the error at degree 14
      is this.", "ExampleText", CellID->200000109],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["Abs[solC[[1, 1, 2]][0, 0] - uex2[0, 0]]"], "Input", CellLabel->"In[34]:=", CellID->200000110],
Cell[BoxData["\"1.242291491898584`*^-9\""], "Output", CellLabel->"Out[35]=", CellID->200000111]
}, Open]]
}, Open]]
}, Open]],
